# Walkthrough - Streamlit Presentation Dashboard Architecture

This document summarizes the changes made to introduce the new **Presentation** dashboard, styled as a scientific conference presentation deck.

## Changes Made

We created a new, modular architecture directory: `c:\Users\maria\Documents\GitHub\fermentation_game\Presentation\`

### Architectural Files
1. **[app.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/app.py)**: The main entrypoint. Configures the Streamlit page layout to wide, injects the custom styles, registers the custom Plotly templates, initializes the state, caches the loaded data, and sets up 6 clean tabs.
2. **[config.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/config.py)**: The page layout config and styling module. Establishes a tailored academic dark mode template for Plotly (`scientific_presentation`) with specific fonts, HSL-derived colorway scales, and axes grid visibility settings.
3. **[state.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/state.py)**: The central state dictionary tracking user presentation parameters across tabs. Tracks active selection filters, themes, and interactive forecast slider variables.
4. **[data_loader.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/data_loader.py)**: Data cache manager utilizing localized caching (`@st.cache_data`) for processing gameplay logs and feedback metrics. Computes secondary features like text complexity and AI text similarity scores.
5. **[styles.css](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/styles.css)**: Academic CSS styling including Outfit/Inter fonts, glassmorphism card classes (`.glass-card`), subtle hover translations, and fade-in entry micro-animations.

### Presentation Tab Modules
Located in `Presentation/tabs/`:
- **[tab_0.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/tabs/tab_0.py)**: Abstract and introduction slide.
- **[tab_1.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/tabs/tab_1.py)**: H1 Coordination Cost (time analysis lines and cumulative bar charts).
- **[tab_2.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/tabs/tab_2.py)**: H2 Delegation Effect (side-by-side length/complexity boxplots, similarity trend lines).
- **[tab_3.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/tabs/tab_3.py)**: H3 Efficiency Illusion (difficulty distributions and correlation scatter plots).
- **[tab_4.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/tabs/tab_4.py)**: Participant Clusters (interactive bubble chart mapping Copiers, Improvers, and Control groups).
- **[tab_5.py](file:///c:/Users/maria/Documents/GitHub/fermentation_game/Presentation/tabs/tab_5.py)**: Dynamic forecasting simulator with parameter sliders and Gauge indicator subplots.

